#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""Relatedness, pedigree and sex QC, from somalier's relate tables and the pedigree.

Three subcommands, one for each place the sampleqc step runs them.

mendelian
    Reads `bcftools query -f '[%GT\\t%GQ\\t%DP\\t]\\n'` of a family's biallelic autosomal SNVs on
    stdin, its sample order from --samples, and writes the parent-child counts the family
    level reads: one row per trio (child, father, mother all in the BCF) and one per
    parent-child pair. A genotype counts when GQ >= 20 and DP >= 10; a site counts for a
    trio or a pair when every one of its members is called there and one of them carries
    the ALT.

      trio   errors: the child's genotype cannot come from the parents' (Mendelian error)
      pair   errors: opposite homozygotes, 0/0 against 1/1, which a parent and its child
                     never are but by a genotyping error or a deletion

family
    From somalier relate's samples.tsv and pairs.tsv of one family, the family's inputs
    snapshot (written by the pipeline: its pedigree rows, normalised, with which members
    have a somalier extract and a coverage JSON), the coverage JSONs, the mendelian counts,
    and the members' extracts with somalier's sites VCF, writes <prefix>.samples.tsv,
    <prefix>.pairs.tsv and <prefix>.flags.tsv.

cohort
    From somalier relate's pairs.tsv of every sample of the cohort, the cohort snapshot and
    every family's three tables, writes the cohort's: the family tables concatenated, with
    the pairs of different families related at the third degree or closer added, and the
    flags only the cohort can raise.

Genotypes. somalier relate calls a site from its read counts, at depth 7 or more: het when
the alternate allele fraction is within 0.3-0.7, and homozygous only when it is below the
hom cutoff, or above 1 minus it; anything between is unknown. somalier's default cutoff,
0.01, makes one stray read at 40x enough to lose a homozygous site, and the more of them a
sample loses, the fewer opposite homozygotes it shows and the higher its kinship with
everyone: noise and contamination read as relatedness. The pipeline runs relate with
SOMALIER_AB_HOM_CUTOFF set to the sampleqc_hom_cutoff parameter, 0.1, and this script calls
the extracts with the same rule.

Relatedness. somalier counts, for each pair, at the sites both are called: ibs0 (one 0/0,
the other 1/1), ibs2 (same genotype), shared_hets, and hets_ab, the two samples'
heterozygous sites summed. The kinship is KING-robust's, (shared_hets - 2 ibs0) / hets_ab:
0.5 for a duplicate or MZ twin,
0.25 for a parent-offspring pair or full siblings, 0.125 for the second degree. The
classes are KING's, with parent-offspring told from full siblings by IBS0, which a parent
and its child share at no site and siblings at about a quarter of an unrelated pair's:

    kinship > 0.354                       duplicate (or MZ twin)
    0.177 - 0.354, ibs0/ibs2 < 0.01       parent-offspring
    0.177 - 0.354, ibs0/ibs2 >= 0.01      full-sibs
    0.0884 - 0.177                        second-degree (half-sibs, grandparent, avuncular)
    0.0442 - 0.0884                       third-degree (first cousins, ...)
    below 0.0442                          unrelated

A pair with fewer than 2,000 sites called in both is low_confidence and is never flagged.

The expected kinship is the pedigree's, by the recursive definition, founders unrelated:
phi(a, a) = (1 + phi(father, mother)) / 2, and for a not an ancestor of b,
phi(a, b) = (phi(father_a, b) + phi(mother_a, b)) / 2. A parent named in the pedigree
without a row of its own is a founder. A parent written 0 is one not in the pedigree, not
someone else: the expected kinship is then the least the pair can have. A pair observed
more distant than the pedigree says contradicts it; one observed closer is related beyond
what the pedigree records - siblings whose parents are not in it, consanguineous spouses -
and is reported as information. Siblings who share one recorded parent, with the other
missing for either, may be full or half siblings. The exception is a pair observed first
degree although both have both parents recorded and the pedigree does not make them
first-degree relatives: that is a contradiction.

Twins and UPD. Two siblings of the same sex observed as one person are MZ_TWIN_CANDIDATE;
any other duplicate is DUPLICATE_OR_MZ. A recorded parent and child whose opposite
homozygotes, in the extracts, mostly lie on one chromosome are UPD_CANDIDATE rather than
NOT_PARENT: over their span, a whole chromosome or a segment, the child has no allele from
that parent. With no het there at its usual depth, both copies come from the other parent
(isodisomy); at a lower depth, the parent's copy is deleted.

Across families, a kinship at the third degree is information: KING's estimator assumes the
pair comes from one homogeneous population, and two admixed samples of similar ancestry
reach 0.08 without being related. A pair at the second degree or closer is flagged only when
its IBS0 agrees: its ibs0/ibs2 at most 0.6 times the median of the cohort's unrelated pairs
(second-degree relatives share no allele IBD at half their sites, so they have about half the
opposite homozygotes of unrelated pairs). A sample with CHARR of 0.05 or more relates to every
other at a spurious kinship: its pairs with other families are left out, and it is flagged
RELATEDNESS_UNRELIABLE once.

Contamination. CHARR as Lu et al. (AJHG 2023) define it, from the extract's read counts:
at autosomal sites of depth 20-100 that look homozygous (minor read fraction below 0.2,
other alleles at most 4%), whose absent allele has a population frequency of 10-90% in the
sites VCF, the minor reads over the depth, divided by that frequency, averaged. It
estimates the fraction of reads from another person; a clean WGS sample is well below 1%.
somalier's own contamination_charr, kept as somalier_charr, calls homozygous sites more
loosely and reads several times higher at low depth. 0.02 or more is POSSIBLE_CONTAMINATION
(medium), 0.05 or more (high).

Sex. The X and Y copy numbers are 2 x the chromosome's depth over the autosomes': from the
coverage JSON of the cnv_coverage step when the sample has one (its chrX_ratio and
chrY_ratio, over whole chromosomes), from somalier's depth at its sites otherwise, over its
mean depth at the autosomal sites it genotypes (gt_depth_mean). The
karyotype is cnv_coverage's rule: each rounded to the nearest copy, ambiguous when either
is more than 0.25 from it or X rounds to 0. A karyotype with a Y is male, one without
female. The X heterozygosity, het / (het + hom-alt) at somalier's X sites, should be near
0 with one X and well above it with two: below 0.1 with two X, or above 0.25 with one, is
X_HET_INCONSISTENT.
"""

import argparse
import array
import glob
import gzip
import json
import math
import os
import re
import statistics
import struct
import sys

KING_DUPLICATE = 0.354
KING_FIRST = 0.177
KING_SECOND = 0.0884
KING_THIRD = 0.0442
PO_IBS0_IBS2_MAX = 0.01
MIN_PAIR_SITES = 2000
MIN_SAMPLE_SITES = 5000
MIN_X_SITES = 50
SEX_TOLERANCE = 0.25
X_HET_ONE_X_MAX = 0.25
X_HET_TWO_X_MIN = 0.1
CHARR_WARN = 0.02
CHARR_HIGH = 0.05
CHARR_MIN_DP = 20
CHARR_MAX_DP = 100
CHARR_HOM_MINOR_MAX = 0.2
CHARR_AF_MIN = 0.1
CHARR_AF_MAX = 0.9
CHARR_MAX_OTHER = 0.04
CHARR_MIN_SITES = 500
HOM_CUTOFF = 0.1
SOMALIER_MIN_AB = 0.3
SOMALIER_MIN_DEPTH = 7
SOMALIER_MAX_OTHER = 0.1
UPD_MIN_OPPOSITE = 20
UPD_MIN_SHARE = 0.8
IBS0_RELATED_MAX = 0.6
MIN_BASELINE_PAIRS = 100
MIN_GQ = 20
MIN_DP = 10
MENDEL_MIN_SITES = 1000
PO_OPPOSITE_HOM_MAX = 0.01

# Degree of each relationship class, for comparing expected and observed
DEGREE = {
    "duplicate": 0,
    "parent-offspring": 1, "full-sibs": 1, "first-degree": 1,
    "half-sibs": 2, "second-degree": 2,
    "third-degree": 3,
    "unrelated": 4,
}

SAMPLE_COLUMNS = ["family_id", "sample", "father", "mother", "pedigree_sex", "inferred_sex", "karyotype",
                  "sex_evidence", "x_copies", "y_copies", "somalier_x_copies", "somalier_y_copies",
                  "x_het_rate", "x_sites", "depth_mean", "n_sites_called", "het_hom_alt_ratio",
                  "contamination_charr", "charr_sites", "somalier_charr", "p_middling_ab", "trio_informative_sites",
                  "trio_mendelian_error_rate", "flags"]
PAIR_COLUMNS = ["family_id_a", "sample_a", "family_id_b", "sample_b", "n_sites", "ibs0", "ibs2",
                "ibs0_ibs2_ratio", "king_kinship", "somalier_relatedness", "hom_concordance", "x_ibs0", "x_ibs2",
                "expected_kinship", "expected_relationship", "observed_relationship",
                "po_informative_sites", "po_opposite_hom_rate", "status"]
FLAG_COLUMNS = ["level", "family_id", "sample_a", "sample_b", "flag", "severity", "evidence"]
MENDEL_COLUMNS = ["kind", "child", "father", "mother", "informative_sites", "errors"]


def die(msg):
    print(f"ERROR: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)


def fmt(value, digits=4):
    if value is None:
        return "."
    if isinstance(value, float):
        if math.isnan(value):
            return "."
        return f"{value:.{digits}f}"
    return str(value)


def as_float(text):
    try:
        value = float(text)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    return None if math.isnan(value) else value


def write_tsv(path, columns, rows):
    with open(path, "w") as fh:
        fh.write("\t".join(columns) + "\n")
        for row in rows:
            fh.write("\t".join(fmt(row.get(c)) for c in columns) + "\n")


def read_tsv(path):
    """Rows of a TSV as dicts. A header starting with '#' (somalier's) loses it."""
    with open(path) as fh:
        header = fh.readline().rstrip("\n").lstrip("#").split("\t")
        rows = []
        for line in fh:
            line = line.rstrip("\n")
            if line:
                rows.append(dict(zip(header, line.split("\t"))))
    return header, rows


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extracts and sites
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_extract(path):
    """A somalier extract: (sample, autosomal counts). The counts are one flat array of
    (A reads, B reads, other reads) per site, in the order of read_sites. somalier writes a
    format byte (2), the name's length and the name, the numbers of autosomal, X and Y
    sites as uint16, then three uint32 per site."""
    with open(path, "rb") as fh:
        data = fh.read()
    if len(data) < 2 or data[0] != 2:
        die(f"{path} is not a somalier extract of format 2")
    end = 2 + data[1]
    name = data[2:end].decode()
    n_auto, n_x, n_y = struct.unpack_from("<HHH", data, end)
    start = end + 6
    if len(data) != start + 12 * (n_auto + n_x + n_y):
        die(f"{path}: {len(data)} bytes, not those of {n_auto + n_x + n_y} sites")
    counts = array.array("I")
    counts.frombytes(data[start:start + 12 * n_auto])
    if sys.byteorder != "little":
        counts.byteswap()
    return name, counts


def read_sites(path):
    """somalier's autosomal sites, in the order its extracts store them (chromosome name,
    then position): [(chrom, position, B allele population frequency)]. somalier stores the
    two alleles in alphabetical order, so where the ALT sorts first the frequency is flipped."""
    sites = []
    with gzip.open(path, "rt") as fh:
        for line in fh:
            if line.startswith("#"):
                continue
            cols = line.rstrip("\n").split("\t")
            if cols[0] in ("X", "chrX", "Y", "chrY"):
                continue
            af = None
            for field in cols[7].split(";"):
                if field.startswith("AF="):
                    af = float(field[3:].split(",")[0])
            if af is None:
                die(f"{path}: no INFO/AF at {cols[0]}:{cols[1]}")
            sites.append((cols[0], int(cols[1]), af if cols[3] < cols[4] else 1 - af))
    sites.sort(key=lambda s: (s[0], s[1]))
    return sites


def genotype(n_a, n_b, n_other, hom_cutoff):
    """somalier relate's call of a site: 0 or 2 homozygous, 1 het, None unknown."""
    depth = n_a + n_b
    if depth < SOMALIER_MIN_DEPTH or (n_other and n_other / (depth + n_other) > SOMALIER_MAX_OTHER):
        return None
    ab = n_b / depth
    if ab < hom_cutoff:
        return 0
    if ab > 1 - hom_cutoff:
        return 2
    if SOMALIER_MIN_AB <= ab <= 1 - SOMALIER_MIN_AB:
        return 1
    return None


def charr(counts, sites):
    """(CHARR, sites used) of a sample's counts; CHARR is None below CHARR_MIN_SITES."""
    total, used = 0.0, 0
    for i, (_, _, af_b) in enumerate(sites):
        n_a, n_b, n_other = counts[3 * i], counts[3 * i + 1], counts[3 * i + 2]
        depth = n_a + n_b
        if depth < CHARR_MIN_DP or depth > CHARR_MAX_DP or n_other > CHARR_MAX_OTHER * (depth + n_other):
            continue
        minor, absent_af = (n_a, 1 - af_b) if n_b > n_a else (n_b, af_b)
        if minor >= CHARR_HOM_MINOR_MAX * depth or not CHARR_AF_MIN <= absent_af <= CHARR_AF_MAX:
            continue
        total += minor / (depth * absent_af)
        used += 1
    return (total / used if used >= CHARR_MIN_SITES else None), used


class Extracts:
    """The members' extracts, called as somalier relate calls them."""

    def __init__(self, paths, sites_path, hom_cutoff):
        self.sites = read_sites(sites_path)
        self.counts, self.calls = {}, {}
        for path in paths:
            name, counts = read_extract(path)
            if len(counts) != 3 * len(self.sites):
                die(f"{path} has {len(counts) // 3} autosomal sites, {sites_path} {len(self.sites)}")
            self.counts[name] = counts
            self.calls[name] = [genotype(counts[3 * i], counts[3 * i + 1], counts[3 * i + 2], hom_cutoff)
                                for i in range(len(self.sites))]

    def charr(self, sample):
        return charr(self.counts[sample], self.sites) if sample in self.counts else (None, 0)

    def upd(self, parent, child):
        """(flag, severity, evidence) when the opposite homozygotes of a recorded parent and
        child lie on one chromosome, or None. The evidence gives their span, and the child's
        heterozygosity and depth over it: no het at a normal depth is uniparental isodisomy, a
        lower depth a deletion of the parent's copy."""
        if parent not in self.calls or child not in self.calls:
            return None
        gp, gc, counts = self.calls[parent], self.calls[child], self.counts[child]
        opposite = {}
        for i, (chrom, pos, _) in enumerate(self.sites):
            if gp[i] is not None and gc[i] is not None and abs(gp[i] - gc[i]) == 2:
                opposite.setdefault(chrom, []).append(pos)
        n = sum(len(v) for v in opposite.values())
        if n < UPD_MIN_OPPOSITE:
            return None
        chrom = max(opposite, key=lambda c: len(opposite[c]))
        if len(opposite[chrom]) < UPD_MIN_SHARE * n:
            return None
        start, end = min(opposite[chrom]), max(opposite[chrom])
        inside, everywhere = [0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0]  # called sites, hets, depth
        for i, (c, pos, _) in enumerate(self.sites):
            if gc[i] is None:
                continue
            tallies = (everywhere, inside) if c == chrom and start <= pos <= end else (everywhere,)
            for t in tallies:
                t[0] += 1
                t[1] += gc[i] == 1
                t[2] += counts[3 * i] + counts[3 * i + 1]
        het_in = inside[1] / inside[0] if inside[0] else None
        het_all = everywhere[1] / everywhere[0]
        depth = (inside[2] / inside[0]) / (everywhere[2] / everywhere[0]) if inside[0] and everywhere[2] else None
        if depth is not None and depth < 0.75:
            kind = f"a deletion of {parent}'s copy"
        elif het_in is not None and het_in < 0.25 * het_all:
            kind = f"uniparental isodisomy: both copies from {child}'s other parent"
        else:
            kind = f"uniparental heterodisomy, or {parent} is not the parent"
        return ("UPD_CANDIDATE", "high",
                "{} of the {} opposite homozygotes of {} and {} lie on {}, between {} and {} Mb; {} is "
                "heterozygous at {} of its {} sites there ({} genome-wide), at {} of its mean depth: {}".format(
                    len(opposite[chrom]), n, parent, child, chrom, fmt(start / 1e6, 1), fmt(end / 1e6, 1), child,
                    fmt(het_in, 3), inside[0], fmt(het_all, 3), fmt(depth, 2), kind))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Snapshot (the pedigree as the pipeline wrote it for this run)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_snapshot(path):
    """Members in pedigree order: sample -> dict(fid, father, mother, sex, somalier, coverage).
    Header lines start with '#'; parents are '0' when unknown, sex 1, 2 or 0."""
    members = {}
    with open(path) as fh:
        for line in fh:
            line = line.rstrip("\n")
            if not line or line.startswith("#"):
                continue
            cols = line.split("\t")
            if len(cols) != 7:
                die(f"{path}: snapshot row with {len(cols)} columns instead of 7: {line}")
            fid, sample, father, mother, sex, somalier, coverage = cols
            members[sample] = {"fid": fid, "father": father, "mother": mother,
                               "sex": {"1": "male", "2": "female"}.get(sex, "unknown"),
                               "somalier": somalier == "yes", "coverage": coverage}
    if not members:
        die(f"{path} has no member")
    return members


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expected kinship
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Pedigree:
    """Kinship coefficients of a pedigree, founders unrelated and not inbred."""

    def __init__(self, members):
        self.parents = {}
        for sample, m in members.items():
            self.parents[sample] = tuple(p if p != "0" else None for p in (m["father"], m["mother"]))
        # A parent with no row of its own is a founder
        for father, mother in list(self.parents.values()):
            for p in (father, mother):
                if p is not None and p not in self.parents:
                    self.parents[p] = (None, None)
        self.depth = {}
        for sample in self.parents:
            self._depth(sample, set())
        self.memo = {}

    def _depth(self, sample, seen):
        if sample in self.depth:
            return self.depth[sample]
        if sample in seen:
            die(f"the pedigree has a cycle through {sample}")
        seen.add(sample)
        parents = [p for p in self.parents[sample] if p is not None]
        d = 1 + max(self._depth(p, seen) for p in parents) if parents else 0
        seen.discard(sample)
        self.depth[sample] = d
        return d

    def kinship(self, a, b):
        if a is None or b is None:
            return 0.0
        key = (a, b) if a <= b else (b, a)
        if key in self.memo:
            return self.memo[key]
        if a == b:
            father, mother = self.parents[a]
            value = 0.5 * (1 + self.kinship(father, mother))
        else:
            # Expand the one further down: an ancestor is always less deep than its descendant
            if self.depth[a] < self.depth[b]:
                a, b = b, a
            father, mother = self.parents[a]
            value = 0.5 * (self.kinship(father, b) + self.kinship(mother, b))
        self.memo[key] = value
        return value

    def relationship(self, a, b):
        """The expected relationship class of two different members."""
        pa, pb = self.parents[a], self.parents[b]
        if a in pb or b in pa:
            return "parent-offspring"
        shared = {p for p in pa if p is not None} & {p for p in pb if p is not None}
        if len(shared) == 2:
            return "full-sibs"
        if len(shared) == 1:
            return "half-sibs"
        return kinship_class(self.kinship(a, b), None)

    def siblings(self, a, b):
        """Whether a and b share a recorded parent."""
        return bool({p for p in self.parents[a] if p} & {p for p in self.parents[b] if p})

    def may_be_full_sibs(self, a, b):
        """Whether siblings sharing one recorded parent may share the other, missing for
        either of them."""
        (fa, ma), (fb, mb) = self.parents[a], self.parents[b]
        if fa and fa == fb:
            return ma is None or mb is None
        if ma and ma == mb:
            return fa is None or fb is None
        return False

    def both_parents(self, sample):
        return all(self.parents[sample])

    def spouses(self, a, b):
        """Whether a and b are the two recorded parents of a member."""
        return any(set(parents) == {a, b} for parents in self.parents.values())


def kinship_class(phi, ibs0_ibs2):
    """The class of a kinship, observed (with its IBS0 ratio) or expected (without)."""
    if phi > KING_DUPLICATE:
        return "duplicate"
    if phi > KING_FIRST:
        if ibs0_ibs2 is None:
            return "first-degree"
        return "parent-offspring" if ibs0_ibs2 < PO_IBS0_IBS2_MAX else "full-sibs"
    if phi > KING_SECOND:
        return "second-degree"
    if phi > KING_THIRD:
        return "third-degree"
    return "unrelated"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pairs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def observed_pair(row):
    """A somalier pairs.tsv row as a pair record with its kinship and observed class."""
    n = int(row["n"])
    ibs0, ibs2 = int(row["ibs0"]), int(row["ibs2"])
    # hets_a and hets_b are each sample's over all its sites; hets_ab is over both's
    hets = int(row["hets_ab"])
    phi = (int(row["shared_hets"]) - 2 * ibs0) / hets if hets else None
    ratio = ibs0 / ibs2 if ibs2 else None
    if n < MIN_PAIR_SITES or phi is None:
        observed = "low_confidence"
    else:
        observed = kinship_class(phi, ratio if ratio is not None else 1.0)
    return {
        "sample_a": row["sample_a"], "sample_b": row["sample_b"], "n_sites": n,
        "ibs0": ibs0, "ibs2": ibs2, "ibs0_ibs2_ratio": ratio, "king_kinship": phi,
        "somalier_relatedness": as_float(row.get("relatedness")),
        "hom_concordance": as_float(row.get("hom_concordance")),
        "x_ibs0": row.get("x_ibs0"), "x_ibs2": row.get("x_ibs2"),
        "observed_relationship": observed,
    }


def describe(pair):
    return "observed {} (kinship {}, ibs0/ibs2 {}, {} sites)".format(
        pair["observed_relationship"], fmt(pair["king_kinship"]), fmt(pair["ibs0_ibs2_ratio"]),
        pair["n_sites"])


def compare(pair, roles, pedigree, sexes):
    """(flag, severity, evidence) of a within-family pair whose expected and observed
    relationships disagree, or None. roles names a parent-offspring pair's parent; sexes
    gives each member's sex, inferred or else recorded."""
    expected, observed = pair["expected_relationship"], pair["observed_relationship"]
    if observed == "low_confidence":
        return None
    a, b = pair["sample_a"], pair["sample_b"]
    evidence = "expected {} (kinship {}), {}".format(expected, fmt(pair["expected_kinship"]), describe(pair))
    if observed == "duplicate":
        if pedigree.siblings(a, b) and sexes[a] == sexes[b] != "unknown":
            return "MZ_TWIN_CANDIDATE", "info", "siblings of the same sex: " + evidence
        return "DUPLICATE_OR_MZ", "high", evidence
    exp_d, obs_d = DEGREE[expected], DEGREE[observed]
    if expected == observed or (exp_d == obs_d and exp_d != 1) or (expected == "first-degree" and obs_d == 1):
        return None
    if expected == "half-sibs" and observed == "full-sibs" and pedigree.may_be_full_sibs(a, b):
        return None
    # Closer than the pedigree says: a parent it does not have may be shared, or related to
    # the other's. Only first-degree relatives who both have both parents recorded cannot be.
    if obs_d < exp_d and not (obs_d == 1 and pedigree.both_parents(a) and pedigree.both_parents(b)):
        if pedigree.spouses(a, b):
            return "CONSANGUINITY", "info", "spouses: " + evidence
        return "RELATED_BEYOND_PEDIGREE", "info", evidence
    if expected == "parent-offspring":
        return "NOT_PARENT", "high", "{} is not the {}: {}".format(roles[0], roles[1], evidence)
    if expected == "full-sibs" and observed == "second-degree":
        return "HALF_SIB_NOT_FULL", "high", evidence
    if expected == "half-sibs" and observed == "full-sibs":
        return "FULL_SIB_NOT_HALF", "high", evidence
    if expected == "unrelated":
        return "UNEXPECTED_RELATED_IN_FAMILY", "high" if obs_d <= 2 else "medium", evidence
    if observed == "unrelated":
        return "EXPECTED_RELATED_UNRELATED", "high" if exp_d <= 2 else "medium", evidence
    # Off by one degree past the first is within the estimates' noise more often than not
    severity = "high" if min(exp_d, obs_d) == 1 or abs(exp_d - obs_d) > 1 else "medium"
    return "RELATIONSHIP_MISMATCH", severity, evidence


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sex
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def karyotype(x_copies, y_copies):
    """cnv_coverage's coverage_sex, on copy numbers."""
    if x_copies is None or y_copies is None:
        return "unknown"
    nx, ny = int(round(x_copies)), int(round(y_copies))
    if abs(x_copies - nx) > SEX_TOLERANCE or abs(y_copies - ny) > SEX_TOLERANCE or nx == 0:
        return "ambiguous"
    if nx == 1 and ny == 0:
        return "X0"
    return "X" * nx + "Y" * ny


def sample_record(sample, member, row, coverage, contamination):
    """The per-sample QC record and its flags. contamination is (CHARR, sites used) from the
    extract, (None, 0) without one."""
    flags = []
    # Over the sites genotyped, so that sites with no reads do not pull it down
    depth = as_float(row.get("gt_depth_mean")) or as_float(row.get("depth_mean"))
    x_depth, y_depth = as_float(row.get("X_depth_mean")), as_float(row.get("Y_depth_mean"))
    som_x = 2 * x_depth / depth if depth and x_depth is not None else None
    som_y = 2 * y_depth / depth if depth and y_depth is not None else None
    if coverage is not None and coverage.get("chrX_ratio") is not None and coverage.get("chrY_ratio") is not None:
        x_copies, y_copies, evidence = 2 * coverage["chrX_ratio"], 2 * coverage["chrY_ratio"], "coverage"
    else:
        x_copies, y_copies, evidence = som_x, som_y, "somalier"
    k = karyotype(x_copies, y_copies)
    inferred = "unknown" if k in ("unknown", "ambiguous") else ("male" if "Y" in k else "female")

    x_het, x_hom_alt = int(row.get("X_het", 0)), int(row.get("X_hom_alt", 0))
    x_sites = x_het + x_hom_alt + int(row.get("X_hom_ref", 0))
    x_het_rate = x_het / (x_het + x_hom_alt) if x_het + x_hom_alt else None

    n_het, n_hom_alt = int(row.get("n_het", 0)), int(row.get("n_hom_alt", 0))
    n_called = int(row.get("n_hom_ref", 0)) + n_het + n_hom_alt
    charr, charr_sites = contamination

    copies = "X {} Y {} ({})".format(fmt(x_copies, 2), fmt(y_copies, 2), evidence)
    if k == "ambiguous":
        flags.append(("SEX_AMBIGUOUS", "medium", f"copy numbers {copies} are not whole: mosaicism, or a "
                                                 "coverage artefact"))
    elif k not in ("XX", "XY", "unknown"):
        flags.append((f"KARYOTYPE_{k}", "high", f"copy numbers {copies}"))
    if member["sex"] == "unknown":
        flags.append(("SEX_UNKNOWN_IN_PED", "info", f"inferred {inferred} ({k})"))
    elif inferred != "unknown" and inferred != member["sex"]:
        flags.append(("SEX_MISMATCH", "high", "pedigree {}, inferred {} ({}, copy numbers {})".format(
            member["sex"], inferred, k, copies)))
    if x_het_rate is not None and x_sites >= MIN_X_SITES and k not in ("unknown", "ambiguous"):
        n_x = k.count("X")
        if (n_x == 1 and x_het_rate > X_HET_ONE_X_MAX) or (n_x >= 2 and x_het_rate < X_HET_TWO_X_MIN):
            flags.append(("X_HET_INCONSISTENT", "medium", "X heterozygosity {} at {} sites with {} X in {}".format(
                fmt(x_het_rate, 3), x_sites, n_x, k)))
    if n_called < MIN_SAMPLE_SITES:
        flags.append(("LOW_INFORMATIVE_SITES", "medium", f"{n_called} somalier sites called"))
    if charr is not None and charr >= CHARR_WARN:
        flags.append(("POSSIBLE_CONTAMINATION", "high" if charr >= CHARR_HIGH else "medium",
                      f"CHARR {fmt(charr, 3)} at {charr_sites} sites: about {fmt(100 * charr, 1)}% of the reads "
                      "from another person"))

    record = {
        "family_id": member["fid"], "sample": sample, "father": member["father"], "mother": member["mother"],
        "pedigree_sex": member["sex"], "inferred_sex": inferred, "karyotype": k, "sex_evidence": evidence,
        "x_copies": x_copies, "y_copies": y_copies, "somalier_x_copies": som_x, "somalier_y_copies": som_y,
        "x_het_rate": x_het_rate, "x_sites": x_sites, "depth_mean": depth, "n_sites_called": n_called,
        "het_hom_alt_ratio": n_het / n_hom_alt if n_hom_alt else None, "contamination_charr": charr,
        "charr_sites": charr_sites, "somalier_charr": as_float(row.get("contamination_charr")),
        "p_middling_ab": as_float(row.get("p_middling_ab")),
    }
    return record, flags


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mendelian
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def dosage(gt, gq, dp):
    if as_float(gq) is None or as_float(dp) is None or float(gq) < MIN_GQ or float(dp) < MIN_DP:
        return None
    alleles = re.split(r"[/|]", gt)
    if len(alleles) != 2 or any(a not in ("0", "1") for a in alleles):
        return None
    return int(alleles[0]) + int(alleles[1])


TRANSMITTED = {0: (0,), 1: (0, 1), 2: (1,)}


def cmd_mendelian(args):
    members = read_snapshot(args.snapshot)
    order = [s for s in args.samples.split(",") if s]
    index = {s: i for i, s in enumerate(order)}
    trios, pairs = [], []
    for child, m in members.items():
        if child not in index:
            continue
        father = m["father"] if m["father"] in index else None
        mother = m["mother"] if m["mother"] in index else None
        if father and mother:
            trios.append((child, father, mother))
        for parent in (father, mother):
            if parent:
                pairs.append((child, parent))
    trio_counts = [[0, 0] for _ in trios]
    pair_counts = [[0, 0] for _ in pairs]
    possible = {(f, m): {a + b for a in TRANSMITTED[f] for b in TRANSMITTED[m]} for f in range(3) for m in range(3)}

    if not trios and not pairs:
        # bcftools' stream is read all the same: a reader that stops early kills it with
        # SIGPIPE, and pipefail fails the task with 141. A BCF called before the family's
        # parents or children joined it has no pair to count.
        for _ in sys.stdin:
            pass
    else:
        for line in sys.stdin:
            fields = line.rstrip("\n").rstrip("\t").split("\t")
            if len(fields) != 3 * len(order):
                die(f"a bcftools query line has {len(fields)} fields, not 3 for each of {len(order)} samples")
            d = [dosage(fields[3 * i], fields[3 * i + 1], fields[3 * i + 2]) for i in range(len(order))]
            for t, (c, f, mo) in enumerate(trios):
                dc, df, dm = d[index[c]], d[index[f]], d[index[mo]]
                if dc is None or df is None or dm is None or dc + df + dm == 0:
                    continue
                trio_counts[t][0] += 1
                if dc not in possible[(df, dm)]:
                    trio_counts[t][1] += 1
            for p, (c, parent) in enumerate(pairs):
                dc, dp = d[index[c]], d[index[parent]]
                if dc is None or dp is None or dc + dp == 0:
                    continue
                pair_counts[p][0] += 1
                if abs(dc - dp) == 2:
                    pair_counts[p][1] += 1

    rows = [{"kind": "trio", "child": c, "father": f, "mother": m,
             "informative_sites": n, "errors": e} for (c, f, m), (n, e) in zip(trios, trio_counts)]
    for (c, parent), (n, e) in zip(pairs, pair_counts):
        role = "father" if members[c]["father"] == parent else "mother"
        rows.append({"kind": "pair", "child": c, "father": parent if role == "father" else ".",
                     "mother": parent if role == "mother" else ".", "informative_sites": n, "errors": e})
    write_tsv(args.out, MENDEL_COLUMNS, rows)


def read_mendelian(path):
    trios, pairs = {}, {}
    if not path:
        return trios, pairs
    for row in read_tsv(path)[1]:
        n, e = int(row["informative_sites"]), int(row["errors"])
        rate = e / n if n else None
        if row["kind"] == "trio":
            trios[row["child"]] = (n, rate)
        else:
            parent = row["father"] if row["father"] != "." else row["mother"]
            pairs[frozenset((row["child"], parent))] = (n, rate)
    return trios, pairs


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# family
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_coverage(directory, sample, tag):
    if not directory or tag in ("-", ""):
        return None
    path = os.path.join(directory, f"{sample}.{tag}.json")
    if not os.path.exists(path):
        die(f"{sample} has coverage {tag} in the snapshot, and no {path}")
    with open(path) as fh:
        return json.load(fh)


def flag_row(level, fid, a, b, flag):
    name, severity, evidence = flag
    return {"level": level, "family_id": fid, "sample_a": a, "sample_b": b or ".", "flag": name,
            "severity": severity, "evidence": evidence}


def cmd_family(args):
    members = read_snapshot(args.snapshot)
    fids = {m["fid"] for m in members.values()}
    if len(fids) != 1:
        die(f"{args.snapshot} holds the families {', '.join(sorted(fids))}, not one")
    fid = fids.pop()
    pedigree = Pedigree(members)
    qc = [s for s, m in members.items() if m["somalier"]]

    _, somalier_samples = read_tsv(args.somalier_samples)
    by_sample = {r["sample_id"]: r for r in somalier_samples}
    missing = [s for s in qc if s not in by_sample]
    if missing:
        die(f"somalier's samples.tsv has no row for {', '.join(missing)}")
    trios, po = read_mendelian(args.mendelian)
    extracts = None
    if args.extracts:
        with open(args.extracts) as fh:
            paths = [line.strip() for line in fh if line.strip()]
        extracts = Extracts(paths, args.sites, args.hom_cutoff)
        if set(extracts.counts) != set(qc):
            die("the extracts are of {}, not of the members with one: {}".format(
                ", ".join(sorted(extracts.counts)), ", ".join(qc)))

    samples, flags = [], []
    for sample in qc:
        record, sample_flags = sample_record(sample, members[sample], by_sample[sample],
                                             read_coverage(args.coverage_dir, sample, members[sample]["coverage"]),
                                             extracts.charr(sample) if extracts else (None, 0))
        n, rate = trios.get(sample, (None, None))
        record["trio_informative_sites"], record["trio_mendelian_error_rate"] = n, rate
        samples.append(record)
        flags += [flag_row("family", fid, sample, None, f) for f in sample_flags]

    sexes = {r["sample"]: r["inferred_sex"] if r["inferred_sex"] != "unknown" else r["pedigree_sex"] for r in samples}
    order = {s: i for i, s in enumerate(qc)}
    pairs = []
    for row in read_tsv(args.somalier_pairs)[1]:
        a, b = row["sample_a"], row["sample_b"]
        if a not in order or b not in order:
            die(f"somalier's pairs.tsv has the pair {a} {b}, not both members of {fid} with an extract")
        if order[a] > order[b]:
            row = dict(row, sample_a=b, sample_b=a)
            a, b = b, a
        pair = observed_pair(row)
        pair["family_id_a"] = pair["family_id_b"] = fid
        pair["expected_kinship"] = pedigree.kinship(a, b)
        pair["expected_relationship"] = pedigree.relationship(a, b)
        n, rate = po.get(frozenset((a, b)), (None, None))
        pair["po_informative_sites"], pair["po_opposite_hom_rate"] = n, rate
        roles, upd = (None, None), None
        if pair["expected_relationship"] == "parent-offspring":
            parent, child = (a, b) if a in pedigree.parents[b] else (b, a)
            roles = (parent, "{} of {}".format("father" if pedigree.parents[child][0] == parent else "mother", child))
            upd = extracts.upd(parent, child) if extracts else None
        flag = upd or compare(pair, roles, pedigree, sexes)
        if flag is not None and flag[0] == "NOT_PARENT" and n is not None:
            flag = flag[:2] + ("{}; opposite homozygotes at {} of {} sites in the family BCF".format(
                flag[2], fmt(rate, 4), n),)
        if flag is None and pair["observed_relationship"] == "parent-offspring" and n is not None and \
                n >= MENDEL_MIN_SITES and rate > PO_OPPOSITE_HOM_MAX:
            # The extracts, from the CRAMs, say parent and child; the family's calls, from the
            # gVCFs, do not: one of the two is not the sample it is named after
            flag = ("MENDELIAN_INCONSISTENT", "medium", "opposite homozygotes at {} of {} sites in the family "
                    "BCF, against {} from the CRAMs".format(fmt(rate, 4), n, describe(pair)))
        if pair["observed_relationship"] == "low_confidence":
            pair["status"] = "low_confidence"
        else:
            pair["status"] = "ok" if flag is None else "mismatch"
        if flag is not None:
            flags.append(flag_row("family", fid, a, b, flag))
        pairs.append(pair)
    expected_pairs = len(qc) * (len(qc) - 1) // 2
    if len(pairs) != expected_pairs:
        die(f"somalier's pairs.tsv has {len(pairs)} pairs, {fid} has {expected_pairs}")
    pairs.sort(key=lambda p: (order[p["sample_a"]], order[p["sample_b"]]))

    # A member related to none of the relatives it should be is the likeliest swap. With a
    # single such relative, as a parent of a swapped child has, it is the one flagged only
    # when that relative is confirmed related to someone else of the family.
    close_ok = set()
    for p in pairs:
        if DEGREE[p["expected_relationship"]] <= 2 and p["observed_relationship"] != "low_confidence" and \
                DEGREE[p["observed_relationship"]] <= 2:
            close_ok.update((p["sample_a"], p["sample_b"]))
    for sample in qc:
        close = [p for p in pairs if sample in (p["sample_a"], p["sample_b"]) and
                 DEGREE[p["expected_relationship"]] <= 2 and p["observed_relationship"] != "low_confidence"]
        others = [p["sample_b"] if p["sample_a"] == sample else p["sample_a"] for p in close]
        if close and all(DEGREE[p["observed_relationship"]] >= 3 for p in close) and \
                (len(others) >= 2 or any(o in close_ok for o in others)):
            flags.append(flag_row("family", fid, sample, None, (
                "SAMPLE_UNRELATED_TO_FAMILY", "high",
                "related to none of {}, all expected within the second degree: a sample swap, or a "
                "member of another family".format(", ".join(others)))))

    attach_flags(samples, flags)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.samples.tsv", SAMPLE_COLUMNS, samples)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.pairs.tsv", PAIR_COLUMNS, pairs)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.flags.tsv", FLAG_COLUMNS, flags)
    summary(fid, samples, pairs, flags)


def attach_flags(samples, flags):
    by_sample = {}
    for f in flags:
        for s in (f["sample_a"], f["sample_b"]):
            if s != ".":
                by_sample.setdefault(s, []).append(f["flag"])
    for record in samples:
        names = by_sample.get(record["sample"], [])
        record["flags"] = ",".join(sorted(set(names))) if names else "."


def summary(name, samples, pairs, flags):
    high = sum(1 for f in flags if f["severity"] == "high")
    print(f"{name}: {len(samples)} samples, {len(pairs)} pairs, {len(flags)} flags ({high} high)")
    for f in flags:
        if f["severity"] == "high":
            print("  {} {} {} {}".format(f["flag"], f["sample_a"], f["sample_b"], f["evidence"]))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cohort
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_family_tables(directory, label, kind):
    rows = []
    for path in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, f"*.{label}.{kind}.tsv"))):
        rows += read_tsv(path)[1]
    return rows


def cmd_cohort(args):
    members = read_snapshot(args.snapshot)
    qc = {s for s, m in members.items() if m["somalier"]}
    samples = read_family_tables(args.family_dir, args.label, "samples")
    pairs = read_family_tables(args.family_dir, args.label, "pairs")
    flags = read_family_tables(args.family_dir, args.label, "flags")
    tabled = {r["sample"] for r in samples}
    if tabled != qc:
        absent = sorted(qc - tabled) or sorted(tabled - qc)
        die("the family tables do not hold exactly the cohort's samples with an extract: {}".format(
            ", ".join(absent[:20])))

    contamination = {r["sample"]: as_float(r.get("contamination_charr")) for r in samples}
    contaminated = {s for s, c in contamination.items() if c is not None and c >= CHARR_HIGH}

    observed_pairs, unrelated_ratios = [], []
    for row in read_tsv(args.somalier_pairs)[1]:
        a, b = row["sample_a"], row["sample_b"]
        if a not in qc or b not in qc:
            die(f"somalier's pairs.tsv has {a if a not in qc else b}, which is not in the cohort snapshot")
        if members[a]["fid"] == members[b]["fid"]:
            continue
        pair = observed_pair(row)
        if pair["observed_relationship"] == "unrelated" and pair["king_kinship"] < KING_THIRD / 2 and \
                pair["ibs0_ibs2_ratio"] is not None:
            unrelated_ratios.append(pair["ibs0_ibs2_ratio"])
        if pair["observed_relationship"] not in ("low_confidence", "unrelated"):
            observed_pairs.append(pair)
    # The opposite homozygotes of clearly unrelated pairs, the yardstick for those of relatives.
    # somalier writes them all up to 200,000 pairs, and a random sample of them past that.
    baseline = statistics.median(unrelated_ratios) if len(unrelated_ratios) >= MIN_BASELINE_PAIRS else None

    cohort_flags, cross, confirmed, left_out = [], [], set(), {}
    for pair in observed_pairs:
        a, b = pair["sample_a"], pair["sample_b"]
        fa, fb = members[a]["fid"], members[b]["fid"]
        observed = pair["observed_relationship"]
        if observed != "duplicate" and (a in contaminated or b in contaminated):
            for s in (a, b):
                if s in contaminated:
                    left_out[s] = left_out.get(s, 0) + 1
            continue
        if (fa, a) > (fb, b):
            pair["sample_a"], pair["sample_b"] = b, a
            fa, fb = fb, fa
        pair.update(family_id_a=fa, family_id_b=fb, expected_kinship=0.0, expected_relationship="unrelated",
                    status="mismatch")
        cross.append(pair)
        evidence = "families {} and {}: {}".format(fa, fb, describe(pair))
        ratio = pair["ibs0_ibs2_ratio"]
        if observed == "duplicate":
            flag = ("DUPLICATE_OR_MZ", "high", evidence)
        elif DEGREE[observed] == 3:
            flag = ("CRYPTIC_RELATED", "info", evidence + "; the third degree is within the reach of shared "
                    "ancestry or admixture")
        elif baseline is not None and ratio is not None and ratio > IBS0_RELATED_MAX * baseline:
            flag = ("CRYPTIC_RELATED", "info", "{}; but ibs0/ibs2 is {} of that of unrelated pairs ({}), where "
                    "relatives at that degree have at most {}: shared ancestry rather than relatedness".format(
                        evidence, fmt(ratio / baseline, 2), fmt(baseline), IBS0_RELATED_MAX))
        else:
            flag = ("CRYPTIC_RELATED", "high", evidence)
        if flag[1] == "high":
            confirmed.add(frozenset((a, b)))
        cohort_flags.append(flag_row("cohort", f"{fa},{fb}", pair["sample_a"], pair["sample_b"], flag))
    cross.sort(key=lambda p: (p["family_id_a"], p["sample_a"], p["family_id_b"], p["sample_b"]))

    for sample in sorted(left_out):
        cohort_flags.append(flag_row("cohort", members[sample]["fid"], sample, None, (
            "RELATEDNESS_UNRELIABLE", "info",
            "CHARR {}: contamination raises its kinship with everyone; its {} pairs with other families at the "
            "third degree or closer are left out".format(fmt(contamination[sample], 3), left_out[sample]))))

    # A member unrelated to its own family, and close to someone of another one
    unrelated = {f["sample_a"] for f in flags if f["flag"] == "SAMPLE_UNRELATED_TO_FAMILY"}
    for sample in sorted(unrelated):
        links = []
        for p in cross:
            if sample in (p["sample_a"], p["sample_b"]) and frozenset((p["sample_a"], p["sample_b"])) in confirmed:
                other, ofid = (p["sample_b"], p["family_id_b"]) if p["sample_a"] == sample else \
                    (p["sample_a"], p["family_id_a"])
                links.append(f"{p['observed_relationship']} of {other} ({ofid})")
        if links:
            cohort_flags.append(flag_row("cohort", members[sample]["fid"], sample, None, (
                "SAMPLE_SWAP_CANDIDATE", "high",
                "unrelated to its family {}, but {}".format(members[sample]["fid"], "; ".join(links)))))

    flags += cohort_flags
    attach_flags(samples, flags)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.samples.tsv", SAMPLE_COLUMNS, samples)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.pairs.tsv", PAIR_COLUMNS, pairs + cross)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.flags.tsv", FLAG_COLUMNS, flags)
    summary(args.cohort, samples, pairs + cross, flags)


def main(argv=None):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)

    p = sub.add_parser("mendelian", help="parent-child genotype counts from a family BCF, on stdin")
    p.add_argument("--snapshot", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--samples", required=True, help="the BCF's samples, comma-separated, in its order")
    p.add_argument("--out", required=True)
    p.set_defaults(func=cmd_mendelian)

    p = sub.add_parser("family", help="one family's QC tables")
    p.add_argument("--snapshot", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--somalier-samples", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--somalier-pairs", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--coverage-dir")
    p.add_argument("--mendelian")
    p.add_argument("--extracts", help="a file listing the members' .somalier extracts, one per line")
    p.add_argument("--sites", help="somalier's sites VCF, with INFO/AF; required with --extracts")
    p.add_argument("--hom-cutoff", type=float, default=HOM_CUTOFF,
                   help="homozygous below this allele fraction, or above 1 minus it, as somalier relate was run")
    p.add_argument("--out-prefix", required=True)
    p.set_defaults(func=cmd_family)

    p = sub.add_parser("cohort", help="the cohort's QC tables")
    p.add_argument("--cohort", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--snapshot", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--somalier-pairs", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--family-dir", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--label", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--out-prefix", required=True)
    p.set_defaults(func=cmd_cohort)

    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if getattr(args, "extracts", None) and not args.sites:
        parser.error("--extracts needs --sites")
    if hasattr(args, "hom_cutoff") and not 0 < args.hom_cutoff < SOMALIER_MIN_AB:
        parser.error(f"--hom-cutoff must be between 0 and {SOMALIER_MIN_AB}")
    args.func(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
